{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0124"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c011): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c011.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0124"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge film-media/film","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/film-media__film.g5.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",114],["+","The screenplay of Rocky was written by Sylvester Stallone himself, in three and a half days, shortly after he had watched the outsider Chuck Wepner survive into the fifteenth round against Muhammad Ali in March 1975. The budget was so small that the family helped out: his father rings the bell between rounds, his brother Frank sings on a street corner, and the big dog that trots beside Rocky through the streets of Philadelphia is Stallone's own bullmastiff, Butkus, who appears under his real name in the first two Rocky films. "],["=",869]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",124],["+","Das Drehbuch zu „Rocky“ schrieb Sylvester Stallone selbst, in dreieinhalb Tagen, kurz nachdem er im März 1975 gesehen hatte, wie der Außenseiter Chuck Wepner gegen Muhammad Ali bis in die fünfzehnte Runde durchhielt. Das Budget war so knapp, dass die Familie aushalf: Sein Vater läutet die Rundenglocke, sein Bruder Frank singt an einer Straßenecke, und der große Hund, der neben Rocky durch die Straßen von Philadelphia trottet, ist Stallones eigener Bullmastiff Butkus, der in den ersten beiden Rocky-Filmen unter seinem echten Namen auftritt. "],["=",845]]}]},
